// S-957 (W5-11 U10d2/t2, §4.5, §18.1; the first form of R-384): the form that the candidate of
// newline_after_bound_question_implicit.onsa leaves, the `?` on the line of its name (`T: Dup +` and `?Escape]` on the next
// line). It is the E0020 of the types stage on the `Dup`, and its candidate takes out the `Dup` with the `+` next to it,
// the two tokens it removes, so that the unit reads `T:` and `?Escape](x: T)` after it, without an error (`clean`,
// S-253). The comment stands after the `+` and before the `?Escape` that stays, not between the tokens removed, so
// the candidate leaves it where it is (§18.1: only a comment between the tokens it removes may go with them); the
// text that remains is in the `.fix1` of the implementation. The main position is the start of the element. A file with
// one unit, so that `clean` looks at the whole file.

pub fn f[T: Dup +   //~ E0020 @13
  ?Escape](x: T) -> U32 {
  0
}
